sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Dev as Member
    participant UI as Dashboard PR page
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant GH as GitHub API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Note over Dev,UI: precondition — the review produced at least one fix<br/>whose confidence cleared the threshold (posted inline, comment id stored)

    Dev->>UI: expand the finding
    UI-->>Dev: original vs suggested lines, Commit fix / Dismiss

    alt Commit fix
        Dev->>UI: Commit fix
        UI->>GW: POST /v1/findings/{id}/suggestion/accept
        GW->>DB: fix in this organization, still proposed?
        alt already accepted, dismissed or superseded
            GW-->>UI: 409 suggestion_decided
        else proposed
            GW->>GW: step-up: TOTP code from the last 10 min?
            opt no fresh code
                GW-->>UI: 403 mfa_required
                UI-->>Dev: enter your authenticator code, then retry
            end
            GW->>GH: get the pull request
            alt closed, from a fork, or head moved past the reviewed commit
                GW-->>UI: 409 pull_request_closed / fork_not_supported / head_moved
            else same head
                GW->>GH: read the file at the head
                alt reviewed lines changed
                    GW-->>UI: 409 file_changed
                else lines match
                    GW->>GH: commit the fixed file onto the branch (Contents API)
                    GH-->>GW: commit sha
                    GW->>DB: state = accepted, resolved_by_user_id, commit sha
                    GW->>GH: reply "Applied in {sha}" on the fix's comment
                    GW-->>UI: 200 { state: accepted, commitSha }
                    UI-->>Dev: Committed in {sha}
                end
            end
        end

    else Apply all fixes (PR page, or the button on the Check Run)
        Dev->>UI: Apply all fixes (N), confirm (says how many are AI-suggested)
        UI->>GW: POST /v1/reviews/{id}/apply-all-fixes (TOTP step-up)
        Note right of GW: from GitHub: check_run requested_action "apply_all" webhook, answered 202
        GW->>DB: the review's open fixes (proposed, posted, reviewed commit)
        GW->>GH: get the pull request, read each file at the head
        GW->>GW: keep the higher-priority fix where two overlap, apply bottom-up,<br/>skip a fix whose lines changed
        GW->>GH: one commit for every file (Git Data API: tree, commit, move branch without force)
        GH-->>GW: commit sha
        GW->>DB: each applied fix: state = accepted, commit sha
        GW->>GH: one PR comment: what was applied and skipped
        GW-->>UI: 200 { commitSha, applied, aiApplied, skipped }

    else Dismiss
        Dev->>UI: Dismiss (reason, optional comment)
        UI->>GW: POST /v1/findings/{id}/suggestion/reject
        GW->>DB: state = rejected, reason, comment (only while proposed)
        GW-->>UI: 200 recorded
        UI-->>Dev: Dismissed — the finding stays visible, no code changed
    end

    Note over GW,DB: Code Sentinel never writes to a branch on its own.<br/>Commit fix and Apply all fixes are the only paths to a commit (FR-GH-04, AC-04).

    Note over GW,DB: The commit is a push, so the pull request is reviewed again.<br/>When that review completes, older proposed fixes become superseded,<br/>including fixes committed with GitHub's own Commit suggestion button.
